WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
The One Piece manga just ABSOLUTELY CRUSHED&nbsp;
our souls by revealing the near conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.080
of the epic battle between Monkey D. Garp and&nbsp;
the former admiral Aokiji on Pirate Island.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.700
And I DON’T THINK ANYONE expected the final&nbsp;
result because, in a shocking turn of events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.980
Garp was stabbed straight through his gut and&nbsp;
then basically defeated by Aokiji and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:26.280
members of Blackbeard’s crew, which could lead&nbsp;
to Garp being captured or even worse killed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:32.760
this battle with his former student. We also&nbsp;
got to see even more insane powers from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.320
Blackbeard crew and a deeper look into the future&nbsp;
possibilities for Aokiji’s role in the story.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:43.560
But can we please just take a moment to&nbsp;
appreciate just what an absolute monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:50.220
Garp is as a fighter. In this chapter, he is&nbsp;
essentially fighting half of an entire Yonko crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:57.180
including an admiral level character in Aokiji,&nbsp;
and he is still dealing massive damage. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.760
he nearly killed the massive San Juan Wolf by&nbsp;
casually tossing the mountain of a man into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.500
ocean. Then he blocks a flaming alcohol&nbsp;
blast by grabbing these random pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.420
and then he even has the audacity to&nbsp;
toss the flaming bodies around the town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.540
like they were firecrackers on Independence Day.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.620
What makes this even more impressive is&nbsp;
that he is doing all of this while at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.140
same time protecting the escaped prisoners and&nbsp;
the other members of Sword while they flee the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:30.120
island. And by the way, I’m loving the focus&nbsp;
on his raw power during his fights and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:35.400
during some of the flashbacks in this chapter.&nbsp;
I personally feel like insane haki and devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.000
fruits have taken over the series SO MUCH, so&nbsp;
it's nice to see just one man popping off with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.040
his fists. Although he's not technically&nbsp;
doing this alone because Koby, Helmeppo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.740
Rear-Admiral Grus also remained on the island to&nbsp;
allow the others to escape. Seriously though, I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.680
pretty sure Garp would have been better off all on&nbsp;
his own. Because while Koby is tricked into trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:04.020
to rescue a random woman, the invisible swordsman&nbsp;
Shiryu appears and is about to stab the marine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.900
Captain. However, we then get to see just how much&nbsp;
Garp cares about Koby because he throws himself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.940
the way and gets stabbed through the stomach&nbsp;
just like Whitebeard did back in Marineford.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:23.340
And let me tell you, this moment literally made my&nbsp;
heart skip a beat! Not only because of the shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:29.700
factor of the scene itself but also seeing Garp&nbsp;
throw himself around to protect someone else is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:35.100
such a monumental change compared to his actions&nbsp;
back in Marineford. Because if you remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:40.020
Garp also cared a lot about Ace because&nbsp;
he helped to raise him as a child. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.420
if you consider dropping him off with a&nbsp;
bunch of bandits solid parenting. Anyways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:52.200
to put all this into perspective, Garp knew Ace&nbsp;
for TWENTY YEARS. Ace’s father, Gol D. Roger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:03:00.300
even trusted Garp to take care of his child. But&nbsp;
none of that was enough to make Garp rescue Ace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.520
which is why it is so shocking to see him&nbsp;
completely put his life completely on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:17.040
line to rescue Koby. I mean, wow, just how&nbsp;
much does he care for this pink haired kid?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.540
We’ll discuss more about that in just a bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:24.840
but first Garp isn’t out of the battle just&nbsp;
yet. In fact, he immediately slams Shiryu’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.900
head into the ground. And while this deals&nbsp;
some serious damage to the former jailor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:36.480
Shiryu gets the last laugh because he knows that&nbsp;
Garp has taken a massive blow. And it’s honestly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.880
pretty lucky for the Blackbeard pirates that&nbsp;
Koby was still on the island because without this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:49.020
deception that put Koby in danger, I think Garp&nbsp;
probably would have definitely won this fight.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:57.660
Now, while the battle continues Garp is weakened&nbsp;
but he still has to face the massive threat of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:03.060
Aokiji and the rest of the Blackbeard pirates.&nbsp;
In fact, at the end of the chapter we even see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.740
Garp bleeding on the ground. Which leaves me&nbsp;
thinking that he might be defeated very soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:18.300
OR we could see him unleash his true power.&nbsp;
Either way, Koby is still there to help him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:24.240
but I don’t really think Koby can take on all&nbsp;
of the enemies by himself. However, since Garp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.460
already sacrificed himself to save Koby, I could&nbsp;
see him take it one step further and do something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.500
crazy like launching Koby off of the island.&nbsp;
And if this is the case, that would leave Garp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:41.040
in a very tough situation, which I honestly don’t&nbsp;
think he would escape from. And if that happens it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.080
leaves us with two incredibly interesting options&nbsp;
for what will happen to Luffy’s Grandfather.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.360
The first and most likely option is that&nbsp;
Garp will be captured by the Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:57.420
pirates. But seriously, good luck keeping this&nbsp;
powerhouse hostage. Sea stone won’t work on him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:02.100
but maybe Aokiji will freeze him or&nbsp;
something to keep him under control. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.240
this option is pretty likely to occur because&nbsp;
in this chapter we even were told that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.340
Cross Guild bounty is three billion berries.&nbsp;
Which is actually an extremely interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.200
number because we also learn that it is&nbsp;
the same amount as a marine admiral AND&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:22.560
you might even remember that it is equal to&nbsp;
Luffy’s current bounty. So I guess this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:29.700
Oda’s way of telling us that Luffy is on Garp’s&nbsp;
level now. Or maybe Garp is on Luffy's level?

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:36.780
I’m not too sure but if Garp is captured then&nbsp;
he could actually be used as the bargaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.880
chip that Blackbeard described back in chapter&nbsp;
1080. Because remember the evil Yonko's whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:46.260
plan for capturing Koby in the first place was&nbsp;
to try to ransom him to the world government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:52.200
in exchange for Pirate Island being recognized&nbsp;
as an official kingdom by the World Government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:58.020
And while that ultimately wouldn’t work with Koby&nbsp;
because he is a member of Sword, Garp might be THE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.940
PERFECT marine to hold for ransom. That’s&nbsp;
because he is basically the most famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.620
marine in the world and he is called the&nbsp;
literal hero of the marines. So if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:12.180
World Government didn’t do everything&nbsp;
they could to rescue him it could turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.260
into a disaster that could cause even more&nbsp;
people to lose faith in their leadership.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.260
But if Blackbeard didn't want to deal with&nbsp;
Garp, an even more absolutely incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:28.140
option is that he could also turn Garp&nbsp;
over to Cross Guild for that juicy bounty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:33.780
and it doesn’t take too much speculation to&nbsp;
think that this could lead us to a reverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:37.980
Marineford. What I mean by this is that we&nbsp;
could have a situation where instead of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:44.760
marines executing a pirate, like they did with&nbsp;
Ace, we instead have the pirates executing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:49.080
famous marine. I mean can you just imagine&nbsp;
the chaos something like that would cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:55.020
with Buggy broadcasting the show to&nbsp;
the entire world? It would be INSANE.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:07:01.380
Though this brings up an even bigger&nbsp;
question. Would Luffy come back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:06.540
save Garp? With all the crazy events going&nbsp;
on at Egghead right now, it is hard to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:12.960
but with Ace already dead, it is hard to imagine&nbsp;
that Luffy wouldn't try to save his Grandpa.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.720
And while it's too early to really speculate&nbsp;
any more about that possibility, the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:24.420
option for Garp’s future is that he simply dies&nbsp;
during this battle on Pirate Island. And while I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.980
personally don’t see that happening right&nbsp;
now, you can’t say that Garp doesn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:35.580
A RIDICULOUS number of death flags. Let's count&nbsp;
them, shall we... First of all, he is a likable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:41.280
older mentor-type character with no super&nbsp;
clear role in the story, except maybe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:47.340
inspire someone. Remind you of anyone. Plus&nbsp;
he is the family of the main protagonist and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:53.280
we’ve just seen him save one favorite student&nbsp;
while battling ANOTHER former student. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:59.880
if that’s not the stereotypical checklist of&nbsp;
Shonen death flags, then I don't know what is.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:05.580
But if we are taking this option seriously&nbsp;
then we have to consider what would be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:11.880
purpose of Garp dying here on Pirate Island.&nbsp;
Is it just to inspire Koby? He did shout out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:18.000
that Justice would prevail, but as a certain pink&nbsp;
flamingo once told us, Justice is determined by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.340
whoever wins the war. So while inspiring&nbsp;
Koby is certainly possible – although a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:28.500
little weird since we haven’t seen Garp and&nbsp;
Koby interact a ton in the story – there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.940
one other option that was hinted at during&nbsp;
all of the flashback scenes in this chapter.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:38.280
Because in this chapter we see that Garp&nbsp;
developed a deep bond with Aokiji and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.420
the former admiral truly respected his&nbsp;
former teacher. And we’ll discuss more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:46.800
about their relationship and what it means for&nbsp;
Aokiji’s future in just a moment, but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:51.960
I wonder if Garp's defeat is actually a&nbsp;
massive misdirection and Oda is trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:57.720
to trick us all. Back in chapter 1080 some&nbsp;
members of Blackbeard's crew were suspicious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:03.480
of the former admiral joining the group, but&nbsp;
killing Garp would definitely show them once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:09.480
and for all that Aokiji is on their side. So&nbsp;
could Garp really be doing all this to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:16.500
Aokiji with some secret mission to infiltrate&nbsp;
Blackbeard’s crew? It is kinda like in Harry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:22.380
Potter when Professor Snape killed Dumbledore to&nbsp;
gain the bad guy’s trust. Although to be perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:28.800
honest I don’t know how willing Garp would be to&nbsp;
sacrifice himself since he wasn’t already dying.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.340
But while we don’t know if Garp still trusts&nbsp;
Aokiji this much, he certainly trusts Koby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:41.220
to be the future of the marines. And I've&nbsp;
always wondered why exactly that is. Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:46.800
it as simple as Garp seeing something special&nbsp;
in the way Koby thinks about Justice? I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.940
Koby will do what is right, no matter the&nbsp;
situation. We saw an example of this in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:56.700
Marineford when he stood up to Akainu and even&nbsp;
recently in chapter 1080 when we saw that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.860
was perfectly happy to work with this ghost&nbsp;
girl if it meant he could continue his duty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:07.860
Or if it isn't just Koby's strong sense of fair&nbsp;
justice, another option is that Garp actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:15.060
knows something special about Koby. I mean&nbsp;
we don’t know Koby’s family lineage. We just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:21.060
met him on this random boat in chapter two, but&nbsp;
maybe Garp does know more about Koby and he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:27.960
a clue about some future special power Koby has&nbsp;
inside of him. It's certainly possible considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.520
all of the new family dynamics surrounding&nbsp;
other characters with interesting hair colors.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.100
Whatever Garp's reason for believing in Koby,&nbsp;
I can’t imagine that the young marine doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:46.020
survive this battle, so I’m sure we’ll learn more&nbsp;
about his super important role in the story very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.740
soon. And if you want to make sure to hear all&nbsp;
about the changes Koby will bring to the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.540
make sure to subscribe to the channel&nbsp;
for more One Piece content like this.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:11:00.000
Now, just like Koby these slimeballs are also&nbsp;
going to play vital roles in the final saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.620
and in this chapter we once again see that&nbsp;
the theme of the Blackbeard pirates is to win&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:11.280
using tricks and deception. We saw it in Impel&nbsp;
Down and Marineford, and here again when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:17.100
tricked Koby which led to Garp being stabbed.&nbsp;
In fact, we will undoubtedly see some sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:24.720
devious scheme when they face the straw hats. Like&nbsp;
they could kidnap a crew member – I’m looking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:33.660
you Ms. Archeologist – or maybe somehow&nbsp;
they get a traitor close to the crew.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.340
Whatever it is, one nearly certain thing&nbsp;
is that Zoro will also have to deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:43.200
Shiryu’s dishonorable fighting style, especially&nbsp;
considering his famous quote back during his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.640
duel with Mihawk, that scars on the back&nbsp;
are a swordsman’s shame. In this chapter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.440
we also got a better look at the powers of&nbsp;
Vasco Shot. If you remember it was recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:57.780
revealed that he ate the Liquor fruit, and we&nbsp;
just now saw him spit out a stream of flammable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:05.640
alcohol that he somehow set on fire. But what’s&nbsp;
even more impressive were these truly massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:11.280
arms that Avalo Pizarro shot out of the island&nbsp;
using his mysterious devil fruit. Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:15.780
what is the deal with these powers?&nbsp;
They seem incredibly overpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:19.380
given that everyone in the One Piece&nbsp;
world basically lives on islands.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:26.280
Though none of that was nearly as impressive&nbsp;
as Aokiji’s mastery of his devil fruit and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:31.980
especially his overpowered haki that&nbsp;
we got to see in this chapter. And I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.700
don’t care about the power scalers who&nbsp;
will say that Garp was already weak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:43.380
but Aokiji’s haki powered fist absolutely&nbsp;
sent Garp flying, so kudos to this ice-cold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:48.420
dude. And even though Aokiji got thrown&nbsp;
back as well, that’s still incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:55.380
impressive considering Garp is likely one of&nbsp;
the strongest haki users in the entire world.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:59.460
That's not to say that Aokiji shouldn't&nbsp;
be thankful to Garp though, because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:05.340
would have likely never gotten to this level&nbsp;
with Garp’s training from the past. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:11.760
in this chapter we see in flashbacks that&nbsp;
Garp trained and eventually befriended a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:17.940
young Kuzan. The former admiral even trained so&nbsp;
hard that he could beat up these old ships on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:23.400
the same level as Garp. But what’s even more&nbsp;
impressive is that Garp seemed to consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:28.980
Aokiji a friend that he could talk to about&nbsp;
his problems. He mentions that his grandson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:33.600
Luffy wants to become a pirate and that his&nbsp;
SON Dragon started the revolutionary army.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:41.100
Wait…hold on this is incredibly important.&nbsp;
If Dragon is actually Garp’s son and not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:46.980
just his son in law, that could mean that…&nbsp;
but I’ll save that discussion for another.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:52.500
Though one thing that is still really bugging me&nbsp;
is Oda is really trying to make us believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:59.100
Aokiji truly wants to work for Blackbeard. Even&nbsp;
though Aokiji’s justice motto is “Lazy Justice”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:03.060
to me he has always seemed like a guy&nbsp;
who wants to do the right thing but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:07.200
he was still searching for answers. And&nbsp;
to speculate on what he might actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.160
do in the future, let’s briefly go over&nbsp;
his character arc so far in the story.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.720
It all started in chapter 321. During this fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:20.700
Luffy challenged him to a one on one duel so&nbsp;
that the admiral wouldn’t go after the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:25.770
of the crew. And even though he easily&nbsp;
defeated Luffy, Aokiji didn’t kill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:30.420
straw hat captain AND he honored the terms of&nbsp;
the duel by not chasing after the straw hats.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:35.700
Then we had a boatload of information about the&nbsp;
icy admiral during Robin’s flashback, where Aokiji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:40.380
was part of the group that destroyed the scholarly&nbsp;
island of Ohara. And Aokiji even appeared to go so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:44.820
far as to kill his friend Saul after the giants&nbsp;
had betrayed the marines. But then in that very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:49.920
same chapter, Aokiji seemed to recognize that Saul&nbsp;
desperately wanted to save Robin for some reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:54.780
and he decided to let Robin go instead of&nbsp;
killing her like he was ordered to. To me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:59.940
this means that he inherited Saul’s dream that&nbsp;
Robin should live. This idea is further supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:05.040
by Robin and Aokiji’s talk outside the banquet&nbsp;
after Enies Lobby. He tells her that maybe she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:09.600
can answer the question of why Saul wanted her&nbsp;
to live, so really he seems to be searching for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:15.180
answers that he can’t discover for himself.&nbsp;
Plus we later found out that Aokiji didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:21.180
actually kill Saul, so there seems to be a lot of&nbsp;
internal conflict for what Aokiji truly believes.

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:26.880
In fact, after the time skip Aokiji left the&nbsp;
marines because he didn’t want to work under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:32.640
bloodthirsty Akainu. We next saw him in chapter&nbsp;
698, when he actually saves Vice-Admiral Smoker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:38.040
from being killed by the Warlord Doflamingo. And&nbsp;
this scene shows us that Aokiji still is a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:43.980
person who cares about his friends and the overall&nbsp;
safety of the world. Which makes it even harder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:48.900
